            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Substitute ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "y=-3-2x",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " into the circle equation and factorise.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=-3-2x\\\\x^2+(-3-2x)^2&=5\\\\5x^2+12x+4&=0\\\\(5x+2)(x+2)&=0\\\\x&=-2\\text{ or }-\\frac25\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x=-2$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-3-2(-2)\\\\y&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac25$,\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=-3-2\\left(-\\frac25\\right)\\\\y&=-\\frac{11}5\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe intersection points are $(-2,1)$ and $\\left(-\\frac25,-\\frac{11}5\\right)$.",
